{
  "description": "Cross-language vector for the EVM-signature → Ed25519 bootstrap. The caller signs the per-case `challenge` message (default EVM_BOOTSTRAP_CHALLENGE='starfish:bootstrap-evm'; an app may pass its own) with their EVM wallet via EIP-191 personal_sign (deterministic RFC 6979 ECDSA), yielding a 65-byte r‖s‖v signature. The signer is verified by recovering the address from the EIP-191 digest (keccak256('\\x19Ethereum Signed Message:\\n'+len+msg)) of that same challenge and checking it equals the given address, then the 65-byte signature is HKDF-expanded into Ed25519 and X25519 seeds via salt='starfish-v3-bootstrap-evm' and the two info strings. A custom challenge changes the signature, hence the derived userId, from the same wallet (see fixture-evm-custom-challenge: same key as anvil-1, different userId).",
